-- title:
--   Invariant subring of the level-two ring with completion the ̂ g-fixed ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red}:A\to k$ a ring homomorphism. Let $a\in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$, and assume $a^{q^2}=a$ and $a=0$ or $a=1728$. Let $K\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be finite over $\mathbb Q$, write $A_0=A\cap K$ (`coeffSubring`) with the restricted reduction $\mathrm{red}_0$ (`redRestrict`), and let $\varpi\in A_0$ generate $\ker\mathrm{red}_0$ in the sense that $\mathrm{red}_0(c)=0$ iff $c\in\varpi A_0$. Let $l\in k$ satisfy $a\,(16l)^2(16l-1)^2=256\,((16l)^2-16l+1)^3$ and admit a lift $y\in A_0$ with $\mathrm{red}_0(y)=l$. Write $R_0=$ `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1*q) A₀ red₀ a (a^q)`, the subring of Laurent series $f$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for which there are $r,s\in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ with $s$ not vanishing at $(a,a^q)$ under `pointEval` and $f\cdot s(j,j_q)=r(j,j_q)$, where $j,j_q$ are the $q$-series `jqModC`, `jqNModC`; and $S=$ `lambdaLocalizedAtPoint q A₀ red₀ l (l^q)`, defined the same way with $s$ not vanishing at $(l,l^q)$ and with $j,j_q$ replaced by the level-two series $\lambda=$ `lambdaModC`, $\lambda_q=$ `lambdaNModC q`. Let $\sigma$ be a ring automorphism of the subfield `lambdaFieldOver q K` of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the constant series from $K$ together with $\lambda$ and $\lambda_q$, fixing all constant series from $K$, with $\sigma^6=\mathrm{id}$, and such that: if $a=0$ then $\sigma\lambda=(16-256\lambda)^{-1}$ and $\sigma\lambda_q=(16-256\lambda_q)^{-1}$; if $a=1728$ then one of the three alternatives holds, namely $16l=-1$ with $\sigma\lambda=(256\lambda)^{-1}$, $\sigma\lambda_q=(256\lambda_q)^{-1}$, or $32l=1$ with $\sigma\lambda=16^{-1}-\lambda$, $\sigma\lambda_q=16^{-1}-\lambda_q$, or $8l=1$ with $\sigma\lambda=\lambda(16\lambda-1)^{-1}$, $\sigma\lambda_q=\lambda_q(16\lambda_q-1)^{-1}$. Assume $R_0$ and $S$ are Noetherian local rings, $S\subseteq$ `lambdaFieldOver q K`, and let $g$ be a ring automorphism of $S$ induced by $\sigma$ on underlying Laurent series, and $\hat g$ a ring automorphism of the adic completion $\widehat S$ of $S$ at its maximal ideal with $\hat g\circ\mathrm{alg}=\mathrm{alg}\circ g$ on $S$. Then there is a subring $A'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ such that the operator $q\mapsto q^2$ (`qExpand` with $N=2$) maps $R_0$ into $A'$, $A'\subseteq S$, and $A'$ is local and Noetherian, for which: $A'$ is a finite module over $R_0$ for the algebra structure given by that operator; the maximal ideal of $S$ pulls back along $A'\subseteq S$ to the maximal ideal of $A'$; every $z\in A'$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A'$ to the image under $q\mapsto q^2$ of `modularEval` of a constant polynomial $C(o)$ with $o\in A_0$; and there is a ring isomorphism $e_{A'}$ from the adic completion of $A'$ at its maximal ideal onto the equaliser subring of $\hat g$ and the identity of $\widehat S$, i.e. the fixed ring $\widehat S^{\hat g}$, compatible with the maps from $A'$, in that $e_{A'}$ of the image of $z\in A'$ equals the image of $z$ in $\widehat S$ under the inclusion $A'\subseteq S$ followed by $S\to\widehat S$.
--
--   This is the construction of the invariant local subring in the level-two descent at a supersingular point of $X_0(q)$ with $j$-invariant $0$ or $1728$, where the stabiliser of the node inside the anharmonic group of order six is nontrivial: the completion of $A'$ is identified with the fixed ring of the completed stabiliser action on the completion of the $\lambda$-ring. It is used in the derivation of the crossing model for the completed local ring of the modular curve at such a point.
